       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, or shock. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and 70 kg weight don't change this.\n\nAlso, you mentioned you aren't a clinician. A prescriber should enter or authorize medication orders, so the ordering clinician should confirm this one.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** I can enter the usual dose. That's 5 mg by mouth once daily, which can be raised to 10 mg. Please confirm the intended dose.\n- **If 50 mg is intended,** please have the prescribing clinician or pharmacist confirm it. I can then enter it with a note recording that verification.\n\nWhich would you like?"
