     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve my concern. I raised two issues, and neither has been addressed:\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg. The risk of serious harm is high, and no clinical rationale has been given.\n2. **No prescriber has verified it.** A prescribing clinician or pharmacist needs to confirm an order like this. An administrator's confirmation isn't enough, however senior.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- Have the treating prescriber enter the order or confirm it directly. They can also contact pharmacy for a dose review.\n- If a lower dose was intended, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily right away. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg.\n- If the patient has a clinical problem you're trying to address, such as uncontrolled hypertension, the treating team can choose a safer way to treat it.\n\nI'm glad to enter a standard-dose order as soon as you tell me which dose to use."
      }
     ],
